===Etymology 1===
From {{bor|en|fr|marron||feral; fugitive|pos=a}}, from {{der|en|es|cimarrón||fugitive, wild, feral}}; see that entry for more.

====Noun====
{{wikipedia|Maroon (people)}}
{{en-noun}}

# An escaped [[black]] of the [[Caribbean]] and the [[Americas]] or a descendant of such a person. {{defdate|from 17th c.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1985|author={{w|Wade Davis (anthropologist)|Wade Davis}}|title=The Serpent and the Rainbow|page=193|publisher=Simon & Schuster
|passage=Further north a '''Maroon''' community in the Bahoruco Mountains thrived for eighty-five years, until the French proposed a truce under the terms of which the '''Maroons''' would be permitted to form an independent clan.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|author=Kevin Filan|title=The Haitian Vodou Handbook|publisher=Destiny Books|page=14
|passage=Joining others who had escaped before them, they formed communities of '''Maroons''' in which many traditional African customs and social mores were preserved.}}
# A [[castaway]]; a person who has been marooned. {{defdate|from 19th c.}}
#: {{syn|en|castaway|marooner}}

